The -tags onnx build's speaker diarization (internal/speaker) runs 3D-Speaker's
CAM++ speaker-embedding model (https://github.com/modelscope/3D-Speaker,
iic/speech_campplus_sv_zh_en_16k-common_advanced), Copyright Alibaba DAMO
Academy (Speech Lab), under the Apache License, Version 2.0, in the ONNX export
published by the sherpa-onnx project (https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx,
Copyright Xiaomi Corporation, Apache License, Version 2.0). The model is not
embedded: it is fetched at run time and checked against the SHA-256 pinned in
internal/localai/speaker.go. internal/speaker's filter-bank features
reimplement Kaldi's compute-fbank-feats (https://github.com/kaldi-asr/kaldi,
Apache License, Version 2.0) in Go.

internal/syntaxnet runs SyntaxNet's Parsey McParseface tagger and parser
(https://github.com/tensorflow/models, research/syntaxnet, tag v1.13.0),
Copyright 2016 Google Inc., under the Apache License, Version 2.0: its feature
definitions, arc-standard and tagger transitions, beam search and English
tokenization rules are reimplemented in Go from SyntaxNet's sources, and the
model files are not embedded but fetched at run time from that repository and
checked against the SHA-256s pinned in internal/localai/syntaxparser.go.

