Model Garden's Hugging Face deployments (#1840, #2148) run, without
CloudBurrow shipping or modifying them, the official images of vLLM
(docker.io/vllm/vllm-openai-cpu, https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm) and
Hugging Face Text Embeddings Inference
(ghcr.io/huggingface/text-embeddings-inference, cpu and cpu-arm64 builds,
https://github.com/huggingface/text-embeddings-inference), both under the
Apache License, Version 2.0, pinned by digest in dependencies.json. The
models they serve are pulled from huggingface.co under each model's own
licence, which the console shows and, for a gated model, the end user
accepts on huggingface.co.

The Model Garden runtimes of #2148 run, without CloudBurrow shipping or
modifying them: llama.cpp's server image (ghcr.io/ggml-org/llama.cpp,
https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp, MIT License); the official Python
image (docker.io/library/python, Python Software Foundation License), into
which a pod installs, from PyPI and PyTorch's CPU index, Hugging Face's
huggingface-inference-toolkit (the server of Google's Hugging Face PyTorch
Inference container, https://github.com/huggingface/huggingface-inference-toolkit,
Apache License 2.0), transformers, diffusers, accelerate, huggingface_hub,
optimum and optimum-onnx (Apache License 2.0), PyTorch and torchaudio (BSD
3-Clause), ONNX Runtime (MIT License), MLX and mlx-lm (MIT License) and
their dependencies, every version pinned in
internal/modelgarden/runtime/constraints-*.txt; the images pinned by digest
in dependencies.json. The start scripts and servers in
internal/modelgarden/runtime are CloudBurrow's own.

On macOS with Apple silicon, Model Garden's Apple GPU (Metal) runtimes of
#2155 run on the host, without CloudBurrow shipping or modifying them:
llama.cpp's official macOS arm64 release archive (llama-server,
https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp, MIT License), downloaded on first
use and checked against the SHA-256 pinned in dependencies.json; and MLX,
mlx-metal and mlx-lm (https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx and
https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx-lm, MIT License) with their dependencies,
installed from PyPI into a virtual environment of CloudBurrow's from the
hash-pinned lock internal/hostai/mlx-lock.txt (MIT, BSD, Apache License
2.0, PSF and MPL-2.0 licences).

